      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm on the fence about this one, if you included Group and Group Public in the list of excluded types, I might have been swayed - But that's been omitted as a thinly veiled attempt to gain moderation control over Group Public lobbies. (Which creates a ton of headaches for the VR events community)\n\nThat aside, I'm not convinced this is a good idea in general simply because I know that this will lead to world creators (Who are not experienced in Trust and Safety) being expected to handle contentious issues / witch-hunts that they never envisioned handling, and are ill-prepared to handle. \n\nThe consequences of (readily foreseeable) poor handling of those issues, in the context of indefinite public world bans that may be shared with other world creators (e.g. United Moderation) possibly outweighs the benefit.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
