      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{618fa6ccbfca2a69d13f829c|full_name}, I understand the concern, this is an idea. I would love to hear feedback to improve it. \n\nI love to watch groups grow their communities within my worlds.\n\nAlso, I forgot to add Group Publics to the post. \n\nMe being apart of multiple great events communities I understand that events are a large part of VRChat. \n\nIt shouldn't be labeled as a world moderation, more of a protection for larger creators like myself. (To mitigate Harassment)\n\nThat's why I believe they should still have access to non Public instances and group instances. \n\nNote: Anything you add can be abused. \n\nExample: Groups gave random people the power to make something.  \n\nWithin those group public instances you could be kicked for outlandish things.\n\n- Not being 18+, Or not having your age in your bio.\n\n- Not being a Furry and being a Furry.\n\n- Sounding young.\n\n- And so many more.\n\nYou are right that some users might feel obligated to \"Moderate\" their worlds. But, They aren't obligated to create a community they would like to protect.\n\nI simply ask for the ability to stop users from hurting my community.\n\nBrainstorm, think of ways to keep communities like mine and others safe.\n\nHave a goodnight- Shadow.\n\nThere's always more to explain~",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
