      "postID": "66124a56cc35d4304d86558b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you don't want certain people in your instance, make a VRChat Group that you can moderate however you please and use Group Public instances. That way you can keep whoever you want out of your instances by banning them from your VRChat Group.\n\nThe [creator guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/creator-guidelines) states you aren't allowed to automatically blacklist people from your worlds, and your suggestion would basically be the same thing. To the best of my knowledge, Public instances are supposed to be unmoderated and open to all.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6638c824ffc24417cef6953c",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "610d538d5303a82960a415b4",
        "alias": "Solar Coral",
        "aliasID": "65c26df1ed6eefce4c5aac21",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/2c95704d7cf1ca3122ea661e51d5f049.png",
        "created": "2021-08-06T15:21:49.596Z",
        "name": "Deantwo",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2024-05-06T12:08:04.134Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "66124a56cc35d4304d86558b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It sounds like you need to work on being better at self-moderating, such as muting or blocking troublemakers, starting a vote-to-kick if they are being a nuisance to everyone, and even leaving instances that make you uncomfortable.\n\nIf someone is harassing you that much in VRChat, you need to report them to VRChat. If the harassment continues even after the bad actors were banned, then tell VRChat again and they can punish them more if needed. For example, only VRChat would be able to actually IP-ban someone from the platform, which would then require bad actors to use expensive VPNs to continue. What VRChat has for legal actions they can take if people are openly bypassing account bans and IP-bans is something only VRChat can answer, but giving you the ability to punish people instead wouldn't give VRChat that option.\n\nIf the harassment extents beyond VRChat and even into threats, then consider contacting your local law enforcement about the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-07T07:25:10.704Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Good evening, I propose a feature to mitigate harassment of larger world creators and smaller content creators.\n\n-Blocks that disallow use of the creators public worlds, this will allow us to remove bad actors that continuously \"Slander, Crash, Harass, and more\". \n\n-This Block shouldn't completely bar access to the world completely, use of group +, Friends+, Friends, Invite +, Invite Only, should be accessible.\n\nNotes- Reports are the way to go, But with larger creators it's really hard to report users over and over again. I thank trust and safety for all they do, But bad actors can always make new accounts faster than I can report them with proper evidence. \n\nBeing proactive and being able to mitigate abuse of users will make our lives easier.",
